<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- The entitlements for the bundled Node runtime (Contents/Resources/node/node), the only program in the app or the Terminal
       archive that needs any. sign-and-notarize.sh gives every other Mach-O none.

       com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
         V8 compiles JavaScript, regular expressions and WebAssembly to machine code at run time and writes it into memory mapped
         with MAP_JIT. The hardened runtime refuses that mapping unless this is set. Measured on a Mac mini M4 (macOS 27.2) with
         a hardened-runtime build of Node 24.12.0: without it node dies at start ("Fatal process out of memory: Failed to reserve
         virtual memory for CodeRange"); with only this one, a 30-million-iteration JIT loop, a backtracking regexp and a
         WebAssembly module run. The native addons of the Harness (koffi, node-pty, sharp, the system addon) load in a dry run, where
         an ad-hoc signature has no Team ID and library validation is therefore switched off for the test; with the real Developer
         ID they are checked for the same Team ID, which they share because sign-and-notarize.sh signs them all (it loads every one
         of them in the signed node before it asks Apple anything).

       Deliberately NOT here (Node's own release is signed with all of them, plus get-task-allow):
         com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory   not needed, see above
         com.apple.security.cs.disable-executable-page-protection not needed
         com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables   we never rely on DYLD_* variables
         com.apple.security.get-task-allow                        debug builds only; Apple rejects it for notarisation
         com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
            Library validation makes a hardened program load only libraries signed by Apple or by the same Team ID. Every addon and
            library in these bundles is re-signed by sign-and-notarize.sh with the one Developer ID, so they match. Add this key
            ONLY if a tester reports "code signature ... different Team IDs" when Strata loads a library that is not part of the
            bundle (for example a native addon an MCP server installs into the user's folder and loads with this node).
       -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
